    </content>    
    <glossary>
    <definition id="def-00001">
    <term>dynamic systems theory</term>
    <meaning>theory that developmental behaviors and milestones are the result of interactions between systems, including those within the individual</meaning>
    </definition>
    <definition id="def-00002">
    <term>fine motor skills</term>
    <meaning>coordinated movements performed by small muscles to manipulate and control objects or perform precise tasks like reaching for and grasping an object</meaning>
    </definition>
    <definition id="def-00003">
    <term>gross motor skills</term>
    <meaning>voluntary movements that rely on large muscle groups and typically activate the arms, legs, head, and torso</meaning>
    </definition>
    </glossary>
</document>